<title>DENMARK: Danish December unemployment falls to 8.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish December unemployment falls to 8.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's seasonally adjusted unemployment was 8.1 percent of the workforce in December 1996, down from 8.2 percent in November 1996, the National Statistics Office said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>				Dec 1996    Nov 1996    Dec 1995</p>
<p>    Unemployment rate    8.1 pct     *8.2 pct    9.4 pct*</p>
<p>    Total unemployed    225,800	*229,200    262,400*</p>
<p>*Revised All above figures seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>NOTE - A panel of economists polled by Reuters had on average forecast seasonally adjusted December year-on-year unemployment of 8.2 percent, unchanged from November.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom, 45-33-969650.</p>
</text>
